The public function `decode_envelope(text)` accepts a string containing one JSON value. Leading and trailing whitespace are allowed, but any non-whitespace content after the JSON value must raise `ValueError`. The decoded value must be an object with exactly the keys `token` and `values`. `token` must be a nonempty string. `values` must be a list of actual integers, excluding booleans. Schema violations raise `TypeError` for wrong types and `ValueError` for wrong keys or an empty token. Empty or malformed JSON must raise `ValueError`. Return a new dictionary with keys in the order `token`, `values`, and with a new list for `values`.

The input string is immutable, and no mutable state may be shared between separate calls.

